'''Burston Incarnon Genesis''' is an item that is used to add [[Incarnon]] upgrades to the {{Weapon|Burston}} or {{Weapon|Burston Prime}}.

==Acquisition==
*Upon completion of [[The Duviri Paradox]] and [[Angels of the Zariman]], and unlocking [[The Steel Path]], players can earn {{Resource|Burston Incarnon Genesis}} from [[The Circuit]]'s Steel Path to place on their Burston with the help of [[Cavalero]] in the [[Chrysalith]]. This [[Incarnon Genesis]] form grants it evolutions to a transformation and newfound strength.
*Purchased from Cavalero for {{pc|120}}, complete with the resources used in its installation. This purchase can only be made '''once'''.

==Incarnon Genesis==
Installing the Burston Incarnon Genesis requires 20 {{Resource|Pathos Clamp|Pathos Clamps}}, 60 {{Resource|Rune Marrow}}, and 20 {{Resource|Maw Fang}}. When installed, the first Evolution tier is unlocked. Each challenge additionally grants '''5,000''' [[affinity]] to the weapon, affected by [[Affinity Booster]]s.

===Overview===
*Incarnon Form is activated by filling the Incarnon Transmutation gauge that appears under the reticule by achieving [[Enemy Body Parts|weakpoint hits]] and then pressing the [[Alternate Fire]] button. '''20''' weakpoints will completely fill the gauge. A full gauge is not required to activate Incarnon Form.
**Charges do '''not''' generate on the backpacks of most [[MOA]] variants, or vulnerability spots generated by {{A|Sonar}} or {{M|Detect Vulnerability}} in places other than actual weakpoints.
**Weakpoints on corpses or [[Invulnerable]] targets do '''not''' build charges.
**Individual [[Multishot]] bullets can build charges.
*Mode switching is '''not''' instantaneous and has an animation equal to the weapon's [[reload speed]].
**Swapping to and from Incarnon Form will fully reload the normal form's magazine.
*Instead of drawing ammunition from its reserves, the Burston's Incarnon Form uses a separate "magazine" with each charge producing '''30''' rounds to a maximum of '''600'''. Once all ammunition is expended, the Burston reverts to its normal form.
**Incarnon Form's magazine is '''not''' affected by mods.
**Incarnon Form is '''not''' affected by [[Ammo Efficiency]] (such as {{A|Energized Munitions}}).
**Charges and Incarnon Form persists through all activities, such as holstering, [[bleedout]], or being [[Disarm|disarmed]]. However, charges and Incarnon Form are removed upon [[death]].

